!SJTU C1-C2 mechanism is developed based on the SJTU_C1_Mechanism. The sub-mechanisms of CH3, CH4, C2HX, CH2CO, CH3CHO have been developed.
!SJTU C1-C2 mechanism is validated against the experimental targets of CH4, C2H6, C2H4, C2H2, CH3CHO.
!References that mainly refered:
!H. Hashemi, J.M. Christensen, S. Gersen, P. Glarborg, Hydrogen oxidation at high pressure and intermediate temperatures: Experiments and kinetic modeling, Proc. Combust. Inst. 35 (2015) 553-560.
!A. Fomin, T. Zavlev, V.A. Alekseev, I. Rahinov, S. Cheskis, A.A. Konnov, Experimental and modelling study of 1CH2 in premixed very rich methane flames, Combustion and Flame 171 (2016) 198-210.
!X. Zhang, G. Wang, J. Zou, Y. Li, W. Li, T. Li, H. Jin, Z. Zhou, Y.-Y. Lee, Investigation on the oxidation chemistry of methanol in laminar premixed flames, Combustion and Flame 180 (2017) 20-31.
!X. Zhang, L. Ye, Y. Li, Y. Zhang, C. Cao, J. Yang, Z. Zhou, Z. Huang, F. Qi, Acetaldehyde oxidation at low and intermediate temperatures: An experimental and kinetic modeling investigation, Combustion and Flame 191 (2018) 431-441.
!X. Zhang, Y. Li, C. Cao, J. Zou, Y. Zhang, W. Li, T. Li, J. Yang, P. Dagaut, New insights into propanal oxidation at low temperatures: An experimental and kinetic modeling study, Proc. Combust. Inst. 37 (2019) 565-573.
!X. Zhang, M. Lailliau, C. Cao, Y. Li, P. Dagaut, W. Li, T. Li, J. Yang, F. Qi, Pyrolysis of butane-2,3每dione from low to high pressures: Implications for methyl-related growth chemistry, Combustion and Flame 200 (2019) 69-81.

ELEMENTS
C H N AR HE O
END

SPECIES

